    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0329" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg269"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 465.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 323, of the 21st
                    ultimo, in relation to the case of John L. Waller, and the papery sent to you by
                    Mr. Hanotaux bearing thereon.</p>
                <pb facs="0330" n="270" xml:id="pg270"/>
                <p>In this relation your attention is drawn to the Department’s instruction No. 464
                    of the 5th instant, confirming its telegram of the 3d and giving the substance
                    of a subsequent interview with Professor Langston and Paul Bray.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
